// A dip, a fenced ember, two seeds on a ledge, two stones whose one-generation rings are ground, a fenced ember on the far road.
name Twin Sparks
rule B1/S
steps 1
hint A new law: cells are born beside exactly one living neighbour and nothing survives a generation. One spark on each stone left one ring each. Rings are ground too. The seeds are on the ledge before the chasm.
tip Drop to the first stone and plant, climb back, grow, walk the ring to the second stone, plant, rewind, and grow both from the far side.
intro The law changes underfoot. Here nothing lived past its first breath, and only the lonely were born. What is left is rings.
outro A spark leaves a ring. The spark itself is gone, and the ring will carry you.
